{"errors":[{"english":"suffer from demon-affliction <term>mei</term> <gloss>demonic influence or haunting</gloss>","image_says":"被魃候 / 有魃病者: the condition is the ba (魃) illness, not mei 魅. The same applies to every later 'demon' on this page.","cause":"OCR","b_right":true,"severity":"material"},{"english":"often manifests with slight chills and fevers that come and go","image_says":"喜微微下，寒熱有去來: tends to cause slight diarrhoea; chills and fever come and go. The diarrhoea clause is lost.","cause":"OCR","b_right":true,"severity":"material"},{"english":"It is not the case that every pregnant woman can control such demons;","image_says":"任娠婦人不必悉能制魃人: not every pregnant woman will cause ba affliction in (another) child. 制魃人 means to suppress others through ba, not to control demons.","cause":"BOTH","b_right":true,"severity":"material"},{"english":"the fine hairs on the body standing up and the hair on the head becoming unkempt","image_says":"毫毛髮鬡鬡不悅: body and head hair sparse and unkempt, and lacking lustre. 'Standing up' is not on the page, and 不悅 (lustreless) is left out.","cause":"TRANSLATION","b_right":false,"severity":"minor"}],"verdict":"retranslate-would-fix"}
